From 0900c3a91e5c77e9c65a07e58756474e3be6e10d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:06:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/39] um: host character device passthrough (hostdev=)

hostdev=<host path>,<guest name>,<major>:<minor>[,drm] makes a guest
character device whose ioctls run on the host fd inside the caller's stub
(STUB_SYSCALL_IOCTL, argument bounced through the stub data page, pointed-to
user memory faulted in first) and whose mmap maps the host fd straight into
the stub (struct um_hostmap, synced around the PTE walk in um_tlb_sync).

"drm" adds the pointer table for the DRM core and amdgpu uapi, DRM-looking
sysfs, sliced waits with guest->host clock translation, guest-page-sized
alignments in AMDGPU_INFO_DEV_INFO and mmap offset cookies, so Mesa RADV in
the guest can drive the host GPU (tested: Samsung sgpu / Xclipse 940).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
