From c56f53b925b8ac2d81a731be8608024667297f25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:37:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/39] um: hostdev: host fds as guest files, host unix socket
 and shm devices

PRIME, syncobj and dma-buf sync-file ioctls now run in the kernel process
and the host fds they produce become guest "hostfd" files (mmap, lseek,
ioctls taking such an fd). hostdev=<unix socket>,<name>,<M:m>,sock is a
connection to a host unix socket per open, with HOSTSOCK_SEND passing hostfd
files as SCM_RIGHTS; /dev/hostshm is a 4 byte host memfd per open. With a
guest bridge daemon and an xshmfence built on /dev/hostshm, Mesa's DRI3
present reaches an X server on the host without copying (tested: RADV on
Xclipse 940 to Termux:X11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
---
