From 9e6f2bebd7106b8fdcdab39f8f386b072af163b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/39] um: clone the parent's stub on fork

A forked mm used to start with a fresh stub and fault every inherited page
back in. Let the parent's stub clone itself instead (STUB_SYSCALL_CLONE): the
child stub keeps the whole host address space, remaps its own data pages and
hands off to the kernel. Fork then copies all PTEs and marks those identical
to the parent's as already synced.

Falls back to a fresh stub plus a full sync when the parent's stub is busy
with another thread. stub_clone=0 turns it off; stub_clones,
stub_clone_misses and stale_fixes count what happened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
