From 8d642c182c8712079f4f25f368bd7165a7200329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/39] um/arm64: fastpath: no fast return onto a read-only
 stack page

The fast return stores x16/x17 below the guest sp while fast_busy is set,
where any fault kills the stub. Another thread's fork() can write-protect
that page while this thread sits in its syscall. Check the PTE before each
resume and make the stub rt_sigreturn instead when the page is not writable
on the host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
---
