From f81dc4c2f7a4c5a2f60798f1e203c170559fb833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:08:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/39] um/arm64: clock_gettime and gettimeofday in the vDSO

In SECCOMP mode a guest clock_gettime() is a round trip to the UML kernel in
another host process, about a microsecond. Make the architected counter the
clocksource where the host lets EL0 read it, publish what the timekeeper
derives from it on a page below the vDSO text (update_vsyscall), and compute
REALTIME, MONOTONIC, BOOTTIME and the coarse clocks in the guest. Everything
else, and tasks in a time namespace of their own, still ask the kernel.

vdso_time=0 keeps the old clocksource and leaves the vDSO falling back.

