From c3eb1fff8bf06898b8da03889361b4b437372e40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:24:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/39] um: install the first page of a fresh anonymous mapping
 in mmap()

A new private anonymous read-write mapping is nearly always written at its
start right away, and that first touch costs a SIGSEGV plus a stub handoff.
Populate the first page from the mmap syscall so the host mapping rides the
syscall's own return. PROT_NONE, MAP_NORESERVE, stack and shared mappings
are left alone. mmap_prefault=0 (core_param, runtime writable) turns it off.

mmap+touch+munmap: x86 UML 103 -> 73us; S24 same-boot A/B 15.3 -> 13.0us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
