+/*
+ * A fresh private anonymous read-write mapping is nearly always written at
+ * its start straight away (a malloc chunk header, a small buffer), and that
+ * first touch costs a SIGSEGV plus a full stub handoff. Install the first
+ * page while still in mmap(), so the host mapping rides the syscall's own
