From 295658ac3d5b94ae53a8c25154d9309f9aba743a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/39] um: map guest pages executable only with VM_EXEC

UML had no exec bit, so every guest page reached the host PROT_EXEC.
An arm64 host cleans the D-cache and invalidates the I-cache for each
new page it maps executable, which made the first touch of guest memory
about five times slower than it needs to be (A1: 52us -> 10us per 16K
page). Add _PAGE_EXEC for user mappings; kernel mappings keep exec, and
the linear physmem mapping in the kernel process drops it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3kysVLGNgK27oVbqXzFEn
